course: dictionary
lesson: 6521
title: Nepali: one word, several jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their job depending on the sentence around them. Nepali can be a noun, the name of a language or a person, or an adjective, a word that describes something. The words around it tell you which one it is.
explain: Read the clues in «"Namaste" with palms pressed together is a respectful Indian and Nepali greeting.» The words Indian and Nepali sit side by side, like two countries or peoples. So Nepali here means from Nepal, a country in the Himalaya mountains between India and China.
explain: Now look at «Nepali food». The word food is what the describing word is about, so Nepali tells you what kind of food it is: food from Nepal, such as momos or dal bhat. A good check is to swap in a clue: Nepal food or Indian food. Does the sentence still make sense? Then your meaning is right.
fact: Nepal is a country in the Himalaya mountains, between India and China.
fact: «Nepali» can mean the main language of Nepal.
fact: «Nepalese» is another word for a person from Nepal.
fact: Nepali is written in the Devanagari script, like Hindi.
fact: Mount Everest, the highest mountain in the world, is in Nepal, and Sherpa guides help climbers.
exercise: What does «Nepali» mean in «Nepali food»? | A kind of dish that is always spicy | A person who cooks | *From Nepal, so the food comes from Nepal | The colour of the food
exercise: Which word beside Nepali shows it is about a country? In «Indian and Nepali greeting» | Palms | Respectful | *Indian | Greeting
exercise: Momos and dal bhat are foods from which country? | Japan | *Nepal | India | China
test: In «She speaks Nepali at home», what does Nepali mean? | A mountain in the Himalaya | *The language of Nepal | A person from Nepal | Food from Nepal
test: Nepal lies in the Himalaya mountains, between which two countries? | Spain and France | Japan and Korea | Egypt and Libya | *India and China
exam: In «She cooked Nepali food for us», what job does Nepali do? | Nepali is a noun, meaning the greeting | Nepali is a noun, meaning a mountain | *Nepali is an adjective, describing the food | Nepali is a verb, meaning to cook
